# 0307 = 0306 plus an optional fixed low (<4 GB) TX GPD ring.
#
# The XNU ADT sets dram-base=0x140000000, so every kmem/BSS ring lands above
# 4 GB (TQHIAR=1).  The vendor TWRP frame has the rings below 4 GB
# (TQSAR1=fec05000, TQHIAR1=0), and the idle TX endpoint NAKs.  This arm maps
# a fixed low page as the TX GPD ring to test whether the QMU high-address
# state is what suppresses the idle NAK.
#
# Switch: ruby_txring_pa=<hex PA> (0 = auto, current behaviour).
# The fixed page is mapped uncached via ml_io_map; the GPD ring is 1 KB and
# page aligned.  Test cmdline: config/0307-boot.cmdline (0xfec00000).
# Risk: the low region is outside the XNU dram; a collision can fail the boot
# (recover via fastboot/TWRP).
# Banner gate: "RUBY USB: 0307 txring=%#x".
# patchset: 312d7a53a0e236f3d0b304857dab03405fd7cc0baee5697b5bdbdc501332af70
